ss -u NONE -l tools/toolbelt.lua run deploy <root> from=<src dir> target=<deploy dir> [approve=yes] [rollback=1] [apply=1]` — the local deployment world (cartograph.deploy): `release` writes releases/<content id>/ (an immutable VALUE; a cross-world create journaled in the target's journal; the same content is the same id, so a re-release is empty), `switch` moves CURRENT (COMPENSABLE: its recorded inverse switches back, CART-1186; gated by the `approve-deploy` DECISION), then the `deploy-health` PREMISE (automated review). Gates: `target-write` + `approve-deploy` (approve=yes, or a remembered decision). rollback=1: a failed health check compensates the switch and undoes the release — the target byte-for-byte as it was. Compensation in general: a compensable verb's `compensate(args, entry)` returns the inverse INVOCATION; rollback runs it through the same step executor. CART-0154 / CART-1186 |\n| Compose write verbs toward a goal and stop ONLY on a genuine decision (a tactic: then / first / try / repeat / each) | `local tactic = require 'cartograph.tactic'; local T = tactic.T` → `tactic.run(store, T.seq(T.step('moveset', {seed_refs, dest}, {'surface'}), T.step('replace', {ref, text}, {'supplied-text'})), { apply = true, oracle = fn })` → `status` done / previewed / stopped (a decision, with `options` + `fixes`) / failed (class, where); `residue`, `work_orders` (every unbuilt stop), `rolled_back`. A DRY run (`apply = false`, the default) CHAINS OVERLAY WORLDS: each journaled step's staged texts become a virtual graph (`world.edit`) the next step plans in, so the whole term previews — `preview` = { [rel] = final text }, `worlds` = how many were stacked, the caller's graph comes back afterwards; a dry `repeat` converges on its own effect; a failed dry alternative drops its world; after a non-journaled step the rest is `underivable` (CART-1160 step 3). FORWARD RECOVERY: a run that stops KEEPS its completed steps (`completed`, each with its `effect`) and resuming is RE-RU